about=hero('Practical software. Clear collaboration.','KS Digital BD brings websites, apps and business software together around one goal: making digital tools useful for the people who rely on them.','About')+'<section class="section wrap content-grid"><div class="rich"><h2>What we do</h2><p>We focus on custom software, website and mobile app development, business systems, automation and digital marketing. Alongside project work, we are developing products for retail, pharmacy, restaurants and sales teams.</p><h2>How we think</h2><p>A useful product starts with understanding the problem. We value a clear scope, readable design, practical functionality and an agreed way to measure whether the result meets your needs.</p><h2>How collaboration works</h2><p>You bring your business context. We work through requirements, design and technical choices with you. Milestones, responsibilities, support and handover are set out in the project agreement.</p><h2>People & project credibility</h2><p>We share team profiles, client references and project evidence when the information is verified and approved for publication. Our portfolio currently provides project overviews without unsupported performance claims.</p></div><aside class="panel"><div class="eyebrow">Our principles</div><h3>Clarity at every stage.</h3><ul class="feature-list rich"><li>Define the scope before building.</li><li>Keep communication understandable.</li><li>Review quality before release.</li><li>Agree support and ownership.</li></ul><a class="btn" href="/contact">Meet Us Through a Project →</a></aside></section>'+convert(section('about'))+cta()
page('/about','About KS Digital BD','Learn about KS Digital BD, our software focus, collaboration process and working principles.',about)
articles=[('planning-your-software-project','Before you build: write a useful software brief','A clear brief turns a broad idea into a more useful first conversation.','5 min read',[('Start with the problem','Describe what is difficult today. “We enter the same order three times” is more actionable than “we need a modern system.” Include the people affected and the cost in time or effort.'),('Name the users','List who will use the product and what each person needs to accomplish. Separate customers, operational staff, managers and administrators where their needs differ.'),('Prioritise the first release','Choose the few workflows the first release must support. Keep future ideas in a separate list so they do not hide the core objective.'),('Describe your existing tools','Mention spreadsheets, websites, accounting tools and any data you expect to migrate. Integration requirements influence both scope and testing.'),('Agree what done means','For each core workflow, describe an observable result. For example: a staff member can create an order, update its status and find it again in the order history.'),('Bring constraints to the conversation','State your budget range, target date, available content and internal decision makers. These details help shape a realistic proposal.')]),('custom-vs-ready-made-software','Custom or ready-made software? Start with fit.','Choose an approach by comparing workflows, flexibility, ownership and ongoing effort.','4 min read',[('Map the workflow first','List the tasks you need to support and the requirements that cannot change. A standard tool may fit a common process; a distinctive workflow may need configuration or custom development.'),('Compare the full cost','Look beyond the initial build or subscription. Consider data migration, setup, training, hosting, support and changes over time.'),('Check integrations and exports','Understand how your data moves between tools. Ask what can be exported, which formats are supported and how access works when a contract ends.'),('Understand responsibility','For custom work, agree source ownership, documentation, deployment access and maintenance. For a hosted product, review the provider’s service and data terms.'),('Test the important journeys','Use a small set of representative workflows to assess each option. A practical walkthrough is more informative than a long feature list.'),('Keep the decision proportionate','A simple website and a complex operational system need different levels of planning. Choose the smallest approach that meets the real requirements.')]),('preparing-for-website-launch','A practical website launch checklist','Review content, navigation, forms, mobile layouts and ownership before launch.','4 min read',[('Check the content','Review company details, service descriptions, portfolio permissions and every call to action. Remove claims or testimonials that have not been approved.'),('Walk through the journeys','Open the site as a visitor. Find a service, read its details, send an inquiry and confirm the result is understandable.'),('Review smaller screens','Check navigation, text size, forms and touch targets on mobile and tablet layouts. Long email addresses and headings should not create horizontal scrolling.'),('Verify search basics','Give each page a useful title and description, use clear headings and publish a sitemap for indexable pages. Search visibility is not immediate or guaranteed.'),('Confirm access and ownership','Make sure the domain, hosting, inquiry inbox and source access are available to the right owner. Keep credentials out of public pages and project source.'),('Plan after launch','Agree who reviews inquiries, updates content, checks errors and handles future changes. A website needs an operating routine as well as a launch date.')])]
